\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  The Son of God, my Light and my Life,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj My good shepherd, my Mighty King!
\par Unto your love have I pledged my life;
\par Both soul and body are for you.
\par I shall no longer tread my old ways;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Place me on your path of righteousness!
\par Protect your child eternally!
\par Gently lead me, infront and behind;
\par Do guide my steps inside and outside:
\par  Alone, I'll take no step at all.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With you as guide, I'll never trespass;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Your word has made me a promise;
\par That Your eyes shall give me direction;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  And your face with me shall proceed.
\par  That I prefer; and I'm delighted;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Your great mercy and acts of goodness;
\par :  Encompass me and embrace me,
\par My resolve is to serve you only;
\par  Of my own free will do I ask you.
\par  To make me pleasing in your sight!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Show me your ways that unto peace, lead;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  And all impediments remove.
\par  Help me to extricate myself from
\par  The troubles of this worldly life.
\par  No words of deceit shall I heed to;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To ever place me in confusion.
\par May I remain awake and pray;
\par My plea is; take control of my soul.
\par Strengthen it, take control of my soul;
\par May I not cease to strive for you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My Lord, count me among your children
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  And make me into a good child.
\par And may your will, the only perfect
\par Become my will eternally.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj May anything that comes not from you,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Or does not with your precepts agree;
\par Attract my eyes nor please my sight;
\par The glory of your majestic name.
\par Is what I always want to witness;
\par My hope is to serve you indeed!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. May I be counselled by your spirit,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj And may I pray to you always.
\par May your words so well stay in my heart,
\par And be spirit and life to me:
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 May I with shyness and with meekness,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Conduct my life while in your presence.
\par Infact, attach my soul to you;
\par May my mind be transformed just like yours,
\par  That I may observe you and your wants;
\par May I always bear fruits for you!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Be it like that, I shall be at peace ;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  Within your love I' ll be at rest;
\par   Your riches and mercies satisfies,
\par  There's no fear nor worry in me.
\par My most precious desires have been
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj That, that celestial town becomes mine.
\par And that to Jesus I belong;
\par O Jesu, draw my soul from this earth;
\par And grant me lasting life from heaven.
\par In you I shall be satisfied.\i 
\par \pard                    \i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

